    "narrative": "For June 28, the Zurich Zebras feature a high-upside lineup headlined by **Junior Caminero** (74.76) and **Yordan Alvarez** (74.67), who represent our strongest offensive plays. **Caminero** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against the right-handed Me. Kelly, with his high SP xERA (4.85) creating a prime environment for production from the three-hole. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a cornerstone start; despite facing a capable arm in Flaherty, his elite xwOBA (.444) and position in the two-hole ensure he remains a top-tier efficiency play for our 5x5 totals. **Trea Turner** (69.55) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.08) are our primary engines for the stolen base category today; **Crow-Armstrong** earns a significant boost due to his matchup against a pitcher with a notoriously slow delivery, which elevates his upside despite the relatively tough 3.43 xERA of Woodruff.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Carson Benge** (40.53). While his projected efficiency hovered near the threshold, a challenging platoon disadvantage against the southpaw Luzardo, combined with a poor SP skill rating, kept him out of the starting nine. We continue to manage our game caps strictly, and **Dillon Dingler** (36.56) also fell short of our 40.0 floor, failing to overcome the drag of a platoon-heavy matchup. While **Kyle Schwarber** (68.77) serves as a key start today based on his .394 xwOBA and favorable alignment in the two-hole, we are monitoring the weather closely for any late-breaking updates that could impact the efficiency of our outfield trio. Finally, we remain diligent in tracking **Hyeseong Kim**, **Zac Veen**, **Rece Hinds**, **Luke Raley**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, **Jose Fernandez**, and **Pedro Ramirez** as they continue their development and wait for potential shifts in the active roster hierarchy. **Gary Sanchez**, **Colt Keith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Christian Yelich**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Kazuma Okamoto** round out a deep daily unit expected to maximize our category output.",
